{
  "answer": "there are two levers here and they do different jobs. Choosing between LRU, LFU and FIFO at a fixed capacity barely moves correctness and moves staleness several fold, so policy is a staleness lever. Whether the cache is bounded at all is a correctness lever: letting it grow without limit roughly doubles the false hit rate, because a wrong answer needs a wrong neighbour to still be resident. Reporting one eviction number would hide both.",
